data.value:
Each disk is copied into a new encrypted image (LUKS, AES-256), which then replaces it:
• the snapshots are lost (a copy holds the current state only);
• it needs free space for a copy of each disk;
• the old images are deleted, not wiped: their data may stay readable on the drive;
• the descriptor and the UEFI variables stay in clear;
• without the password, the data cannot be recovered. Nobody can reset it.
